  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600206",
      "title": "Migrating Everything To Redux Toolkit",
      "sourceHash": "b37318ab7789fbec5f24cb318461aa75a58590ebe4224403d16e1b89ce4cda31",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.3,
          "en": "Now for dispatching actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.3,
          "end": 6.68,
          "en": "createSlice has got us covered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.68,
          "end": 11.57,
          "en": "It automatically creates unique action identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.57,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "for our different reducers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 17.12,
          "en": "To get hold of these action identifiers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.12,
          "end": 21.263,
          "en": "we can use our counterSlice and access dot actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 26.32,
          "en": "That is then an object full of keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.32,
          "end": 30.25,
          "en": "where the the key names, increment, decrement, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.25,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "Match the method names we have in our createSlice function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 37.55,
          "en": "in the reducers area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.55,
          "end": 42.53,
          "en": "Now we can access those keys on this actions object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.53,
          "end": 46.07,
          "en": "And with that we don't access the reducer methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.07,
          "end": 49.66,
          "en": "to find up there but instead we get methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.66,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "created automatically by Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 58.22,
          "en": "which when called will create action objects for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.743,
          "end": 62.56,
          "en": "These methods on the actions object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 62.56,
          "end": 66.717,
          "en": "which we can call will create action objects for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 66.717,
          "end": 70.39,
          "en": "Therefore these methods are called action creators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 70.39,
          "end": 72.88,
          "en": "and they will create action objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 72.88,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "for us where these objects already have a type property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.96000000000001,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "with a unique identifier per action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 85.19,
          "en": "Automatically created behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 85.19,
          "end": 89.8,
          "en": "So we don't have to worry about action identifiers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.8,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "We don't have to create those action objects on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 97.36,
          "en": "We can tap into this actions key into this actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 97.36,
          "end": 100.06,
          "en": "object on our createSlice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 100.06,
          "end": 103.172,
          "en": "and execute these action creator methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 103.172,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "which with their name match our reducer methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 111.43,
          "en": "to dispatch actions, which will then ultimately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 111.43,
          "end": 114.36,
          "en": "trigger those different reducer methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.36,
          "end": 115.818,
          "en": "That's how this works now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 115.818,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "And that means that we, as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 123.74,
          "en": "don't have to worry about creating action objects on our own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 123.76,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "and about coming up with unique identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 129.483,
          "en": "and about avoiding typos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.42,
          "end": 132.89,
          "en": "So that means that what we could do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.89,
          "end": 134.781,
          "en": "is at the bottom of this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 134.781,
          "end": 139.6,
          "en": "we get our counter actions like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.6,
          "end": 144.6,
          "en": "And we then for example, export our counter actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.89,
          "end": 147.11,
          "en": "So we don't just export the store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.11,
          "end": 150.36,
          "en": "but also our counter actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.36,
          "end": 154.02,
          "en": "And by doing this we can then go to the component where we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 154.02,
          "end": 158.14,
          "en": "need the actions in this case to counter JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 158.14,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "and import from our index JS file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 164.45,
          "end": 167.35,
          "en": "and import the counter actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.35,
          "end": 170.3,
          "en": "which we just exported there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.3,
          "end": 175.3,
          "en": "And now, again that's an object which has our reducer names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 176.2,
          "end": 179.737,
          "en": "our reducer method names as keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 179.737,
          "end": 182.94,
          "en": "So now if we want to dispatch an action here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 182.94,
          "end": 187.94,
          "en": "all we have to do is we have to access counter actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 191.38,
          "en": "And then for example, here, increment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 191.38,
          "end": 194.9,
          "en": "and actually execute this as a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 194.9,
          "end": 197.68,
          "en": "because increment is a method which when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 197.68,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "executed creates a full action object with the type set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 208.93,
          "en": "to this automatically created unique action identifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 208.93,
          "end": 212.39,
          "en": "So we get a full action object automatically created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 212.39,
          "end": 213.333,
          "en": "for us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 214.51,
          "end": 215.65,
          "en": "And I also want to do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 215.65,
          "end": 220.223,
          "en": "for a detriment, counterActions.detriment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 221.36,
          "end": 226.36,
          "en": "and all the four toggle of course, toggle a counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 227.26,
          "end": 229.1,
          "en": "The question just is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 229.1,
          "end": 233.52,
          "en": "what do we do here when we also need a payload?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 233.52,
          "end": 237.37,
          "en": "And the answer is we still use our account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 237.37,
          "end": 241.01,
          "en": "or actions and then use this automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 241.01,
          "end": 244.624,
          "en": "generated action creator method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 244.624,
          "end": 249.624,
          "en": "But then to this method, we pass our payload data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 250.76,
          "end": 251.76,
          "en": "So for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 251.76,
          "end": 255.63,
          "en": "an object with any property value pairs of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 255.63,
          "end": 259.053,
          "en": "or just the number by which we want to increase here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 260.05,
          "end": 264.18,
          "en": "So any kind of value can be passed to increase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 264.18,
          "end": 267.14,
          "en": "The only important thing to know here is how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 267.14,
          "end": 269.53,
          "en": "you then extract that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 274.501,
          "en": "because what Redux Toolkit will do for us here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 274.501,
          "end": 279.26,
          "en": "is it will automatically create action objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 279.26,
          "end": 281.86,
          "en": "which dispatches where the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 281.86,
          "end": 285.35,
          "en": "is some unique identifier generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 285.35,
          "end": 289.92,
          "en": "by Redux toolkit and any value you pass here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 289.92,
          "end": 294.7,
          "en": "As an argument to this action method you're executing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 294.7,
          "end": 299.163,
          "en": "will it be stored in an extra field named payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 300.31,
          "end": 302.86,
          "en": "And that field name is not up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 302.86,
          "end": 306.733,
          "en": "That's the default Redux Toolkit uses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 307.67,
          "end": 310.51,
          "en": "Hence now in our index JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 310.51,
          "end": 314.27,
          "en": "in the intrigue is reducer instead of action amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 314.27,
          "end": 318.21,
          "en": "We now need to access action on payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 318.21,
          "end": 321.73,
          "en": "because that is the name off the property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 321.73,
          "end": 325.98,
          "en": "which will hold any extra data you might be dispatching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 327.12,
          "end": 329.75,
          "en": "but with that was a lot of work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 329.75,
          "end": 330.7,
          "en": "But with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 330.7,
          "end": 335.14,
          "en": "if we save all the files if you reload your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 335.14,
          "end": 337.73,
          "en": "we can now use it as we did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 337.73,
          "end": 340.61,
          "en": "And everything works the way it did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 340.61,
          "end": 344.51,
          "en": "But now with help of Redux Toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 344.51,
          "end": 349.17,
          "en": "and this was certainly a bit of work to translate our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 349.17,
          "end": 352.90999999999997,
          "en": "to refactor our code, to use Redux Toolkit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 352.90999999999997,
          "end": 354.75,
          "en": "However, it also took quite long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 354.75,
          "end": 358.92,
          "en": "because I tried my best to explain it in depth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 358.92,
          "end": 361.874,
          "en": "But now that we did transform our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 361.874,
          "end": 366.874,
          "en": "it's shorter, it's more concise and it's easier to maintain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 367.35,
          "end": 370.86,
          "en": "And it's also easier to now work with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 370.86,
          "end": 373.72,
          "en": "If you have a more complex application",
